// Namespace DSL example — see .claude/commands/build-authz-service.md §5.
// `member`'s subject types are `user | group#member` — a group's member set
// can itself be a subject of another group's member set, which is what
// makes nested group membership possible: group:eng#member can be a
// subject of group:all-eng#member without either group namespace needing
// any special-cased recursion of its own. `view` exists mainly to give
// `group` at least one permission, analogous to document/folder/org, rather
// than being a relation-only namespace.
namespace group {
  relation member: user | group#member

  permission view = member
}
